      "range": "[1.0.0.115, )"
    },
    "message": "Previous versions of this package used string as the identifier type. While this approach provided flexibility, it introduced performance concerns—particularly with database indexing and query efficiency.\n\nStarting from the current version, identifier types have been changed to Guid. This change improves indexing performance, reduces storage overhead, and enhances overall database efficiency compared to string-based keys.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other"
    ]
  },
  "description": "SharedKernel is a foundational .NET library that provides essential building blocks for Domain-Driven Design (DDD) and Clean Architecture patterns. It includes:\n\n\t\t\tCQRS interfaces (ICommand<T>, ICommandHandler<TCommand, TResult>) designed for use with MediatR-style command/query handling.\n\n\t\t\tDomain modeling support with base classes like BaseEntity and DomainEventBase, enabling aggregate root and domain event management.\n\n\t\t\tA generic IDomainEventDispatcher interface to decouple event publishing from the domain layer.\n\n\t\t\tReusable application exceptions, including RecordNotFoundException and DomainException, for consistent error handling across projects.\n\n\t\t\tCommon DTOs like BaseResponseDTO<T> to simplify API responses and result wrapping.\n\n\t\t\tA collection of core utilities and abstractions to standardize and accelerate backend development across multiple .NET applications.\n\n\t\t\tPerfect for teams adopting DDD and CQRS with EF Core, SharedKernel helps enforce consistency, improve modularity, and reduce duplication across services.",
  "id": "Sortex.SharedKernel",
